Files in this folder are based on cairo-1.9.4.

Original source archives are available from <http://www.cairographics.org>

The PDF surface carries LiveCode's additions for revPDFPrinter (links,
anchors, bookmarks, metadata): src/cairo-pdf-ext*, and the parts of
cairo-pdf.h, cairo-pdf-surface.c, cairo-pdf-surface-private.h,
cairo-surface.c and cairo-image-info* in src/ between "begin revpdfprinter
additions" and "end revpdfprinter additions".

One local change, marked "OXT-Beyond" in the source:

- In src/cairo-pdf-surface.c, the array of a document's URI actions is
  made for the cairo_pdf_value_t each action is, where it was made for a
  cairo_pdf_object_t (a long). It kept 8 bytes of each 72-byte action on
  64-bit Linux, so the lookup for a document's second link read its
  action type and URI from memory past the first action, and crashed in
  strcmp when that memory was zero. On rc.6.4 under Linux, every PDF
  tried with more than one link crashed the engine (two print links on a
  page or on two pages, and a field with two runs of link text); a PDF
  with one link is the same as before but for its creation date.
